/// queue a block on the main queue and call the manager inside it (the C ABI entry points of
/// 2.0.0 do so, with <code>MainActor.assumeIsolated</code>). The one exception is <code>cancelLoad(_:)</code>, which
/// is <code>nonisolated</code>: call it from any thread. <code>shared</code> itself is read on the main actor, so
/// from another thread call the static form, <code>IosClipboardManager.cancelLoad(box)</code>.
/// <h2>API shape</h2>
/// <ul>
