///     P-1〜P-11 (data-bearing operations) offer both a callback form and an <code>async throws</code> native
///     form. <code>loadItem</code> also has a callback form that takes a <code>RequestBox</code>
///     (<code>loadItem(_:scope:requestBox:completion:)</code>), cancelled with <code>cancelLoad(_:)</code>.
///   </li>
///   <li>
///     P-12〜P-16 (<code>cancelAllLoads</code>, <code>startObserving</code>, <code>stopObserving</code>, <code>checkForegroundChange</code>,
///     <code>makePasteControl</code>) and <code>cancelLoad(_:)</code> complete synchronously and therefore have a
///     single, synchronous form only (see <code>common.md</code>’s “同期 control / factory API” exception).
///   </li>
/// </ul>
/// <h2>Cancelling a load</h2>
/// | Way | Cancels | Thread | Result of the cancelled load |
/// |—|—|—|—|
/// | <code>cancelLoad(_:)</code> | The load of one <code>RequestBox</code> (also before it starts) | Any | <code>CLIPBOARD_CANCELLED</code>, once |
/// | <code>cancel()</code> of the <code>ClipboardLoadToken</code> that <code>loadItem(_:scope:completion:)</code> returns | That load | Main actor | <code>CLIPBOARD_CANCELLED</code>, once |
/// | Cancelling the task of the <code>async</code> <code>loadItem(_:scope:)</code> | That load | Any | Throws <code>ClipboardError.cancelled</code> |
/// | <code>cancelAllLoads()</code> | Every pending load of this manager, of all three forms | Main actor | <code>CLIPBOARD_CANCELLED</code> (or <code>ClipboardError.cancelled</code>), once each |
/// <h2>Errors</h2>
