/// The manager is <code>Sendable</code> and may be called from any thread. Every <code>completion</code> of an
/// operation is invoked on the main thread (main actor), exactly once, on every path, and always
/// asynchronously (also when the operation is started on the main thread). The completion types are
/// <code>@MainActor @Sendable</code>: <code>@Sendable</code> because the closure is carried from the calling thread to
/// the main actor, and <code>@MainActor</code> to state in the type where it runs, so that a closure written
/// on the main actor (for example in a SwiftUI view) can use main-actor state directly.
/// <code>responses</code> and <code>settingsRequests</code> can be read on any thread; their listeners are added,
/// removed and called on the main actor. <code>launchResponse()</code> is main actor only.
/// <code>installDelegate()</code> does its work on the main thread only; <code>isDelegateInstalled</code> can be
/// read on any thread. The deprecated <code>onActionReceived</code> and <code>onTextInputActionReceived</code> are
/// called on the main thread, after the delegate’s
