/// <code>Log</code> is kept so that existing callers still build, and it behaves as before: every call
/// is a <code>print</code>, in Debug and in Release builds, and nothing is redacted. Do not pass secret
/// values (passwords, input text, message contents) to it.
/// <h2>Thread Safety</h2>
/// Methods are static and perform a simple <code>print</code>, which is thread-safe for individual lines.
/// Ordering across threads is not guaranteed.
/// <h2>Severity Mapping</h2>
/// <ul>
///   <li>
///     <code>d</code> – Debug (verbose, development only insight)
///   </li>
///   <li>
///     <code>i</code> – Info (normal operational messages)
///   </li>
///   <li>
///     <code>w</code> – Warning (recoverable or suspicious conditions)
///   </li>
///   <li>
///     <code>e</code> – Error (failures requiring attention)
///   </li>
/// </ul>
/// <h2>Migration</h2>
/// \code
/// import os
///
/// private let logger = Logger(subsystem: "com.example.app", category: "Networking")
///
/// logger.debug("Request started, id: \(requestID, privacy: .public)")
///
/// \endcode
